micropython.h and micropython-amalgam.c are generated and hold the release's sources
unmodified. micropython.h is every header adm_mpy.c needs (py/runtime.h and what it reaches),
with the configuration (mpconfigport.h, mphalport.h in this folder) and the headers the
release's build generates from it (qstrdefs.generated.h, moduledefs.h, root_pointers.h,
mpversion.h) inlined. micropython-amalgam.c is py/*.c, extmod/modjson.c, modre.c (with
lib/re1.5), modheapq.c, modbinascii.c, modrandom.c and shared/runtime/gchelper_generic.c, in
that order. A header with an include guard is inlined where first included; the qstr and grammar
tables, which MicroPython reads several times under different macros, every time. After each
source the macros it defined are undefined, and modbinascii.c's bytes_fromhex_obj, a file-local
name objstr.c also uses, is renamed with a #define around the file. Both files set hidden
visibility after the C library's headers, so MicroPython stays inside the program, and define
NDEBUG.

Left out by the configuration: files, the os, time, select, asyncio, machine, hashlib, deflate
and platform modules, the native emitters, threads, the REPL.

To regenerate, in a scratch folder holding copies of mpconfigport.h and mphalport.h:
    make -f <here>/genhdr.mk MICROPYTHON_TOP=<micropython-1.29.0> BUILD=build
    python3 <here>/amalgam.py <micropython-1.29.0> build/genhdr <here>
The first step needs python3 and a C compiler; a change to mpconfigport.h or qstrdefsport.h
(the names adm_mpy.c adds) needs both steps.

adm_mpy.c, amalgam.py, genhdr.mk, mpconfigport.h, mphalport.h and qstrdefsport.h in this
folder are not part of MicroPython.
